=====Usage notes=====
Using {{m|en|x}} (in upper- or lower-case, italicized or not, and sometimes rotated 90 degrees) to indicate multiplication was common in 17th-century mathematical texts.<ref>{{cite-journal|last=Cajori|first=Florian|title=The Cross X as a Symbol for Multiplication|url=https://www.nature.com/articles/094363c0|journal=Nature|volume=94|year=1914|month=December|pages=363–364|doi=10.1038/094363c0|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240314091150/https://www.nature.com/articles/094363c0|archivedate=14 March 2024}}</ref> Today, this usage is considered poor typography, but it is nevertheless common because computer keyboards lack a {{angbr|×}} key.

